# OxyDrop

**A phone-camera check for a drop in your blood oxygen from your own baseline. No extra hardware, no install, no video leaves the phone.**

**Live app:** https://aravhawk.github.io/oxydrop/ (open on a phone; "Watch a recorded demo" works with no camera) · **Paper-style write-up:** [WHITEPAPER.md](WHITEPAPER.md) ([PDF](WHITEPAPER.pdf)) · **Model card:** [MODEL.md](MODEL.md)

> **Headline, stated plainly: the pre-registered primary metric (P1, detecting SpO2 below 90 on six held-out people) was not beaten.** The previous engine (now behind `?engine=hybrid`), the fixed hybrid pipeline R, scores {{hy:default_R:tm_bacc|full}} against {{b1:chain_v1:tm_bacc|full}} for the best baseline, the shipped logistic chain (a tie). That {{hy:default_R:tm_bacc}} is **optimistic**: pipeline R was chosen after its outer-fold scores had been seen. The unbiased estimate for the whole selection procedure is the nested {{hy:HYBRID_FINAL:tm_bacc|full}}. **The simpler chain has the higher point estimates**: a chain refit with the same levers and no CNN scores {{hy:CHAIN_SAME_LEVERS:tm_bacc}}, and at the same conformal level the chain-only control answers {{cf:chain_v1/0.1:coverage|pct}} of windows at {{cf:chain_v1/0.1:acc|pct}} accuracy against {{cf:deployed_R/0.1:coverage|pct}} at {{cf:deployed_R/0.1:acc|pct}} for the deployed hybrid. All of these intervals overlap, so it is a tie, and the CNN alone ties as well. What held: the CNN beating the weaker baselines (clock, ratio-of-ratios), a calibrated three-state hybrid that runs on the device (ML is the app's core path by design, not because it wins), an open pre-registered leave-one-person-out audit, and an exploratory heart-rate gain (P2, within 5 bpm {{hp:all/HYBRID_agree:within5_full}} against {{hp:all/v2_spectral_acf__forced:within5_full}}) that is **post hoc and comes from BUT PPG**, not a clean win (see below).

> **Round 3, the model the app runs now: PhotonDistill v2, one small trained network. It is on par with the logistic chain on clean light and does not beat it** ({{ph:distill2:0|full}} against {{ph:chain_v1:0|full}} on the photon harness, paired {{ph:distill2:0|d}}, an interval that includes zero, {{ph:distill2:0|nb}} people better) and is more robust under a *simulated* distant flash (out-of-family stress X1: {{ph:distill2:X1}} against {{ph:chain_v1:X1}}, paired {{ph:distill2:X1|d}}). It replaced round 2's PhotonDistill ({{ph:distill:0}}, which lost to the chain) under a rule fixed before any round-3 score; round-3 models were designed after the earlier results were seen, its last files arrived one minute after the stated cutoff, and a three-number colour control is nearly as robust. A rerun of the same code on a GPU scored {{ph:distill2_gpu:0|full}} on clean light (paired {{ph:distill2_gpu:0|d}}) against {{ph:distill2:0}} on the locked run; we report that gap as seed variance. Details and every disclosure: [MODEL.md](MODEL.md) section 0.

> **This project is a prototype and is not medical advice.** It does not measure SpO2, is not a medical device, and the key low-oxygen result rests on only six people. Never use it instead of a pulse oximeter or a clinician. Built for the Veritas AI International High School Hackathon 2026, Health track.

## Who it is for, and input to output

**For** people with COVID-19, COPD, asthma or at altitude who own a phone but no pulse oximeter, and for low-resource clinics. **Input:** a fingertip over the rear camera and flash for 30 to 60 s, reduced on the phone to per-frame mean R, G, B and frame timestamps. **Output:** after a 60 s calibration of *your own* normal (first answer at 70 s), every 2 s one of three results, with exactly these words:

| State | Text on screen | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| Normal | **Normal vs your baseline** | Heart-rate, pulse-shape and light-absorption changes from your own first minute look like the normal group. It cannot tell whether you were already low during that first minute (**oxygen status at start unknown**) |
| Possible low oxygen | **Possible low oxygen: re-check with a pulse oximeter** | Looks like the low-oxygen group (SpO2 < 90% in the study). Not a diagnosis |
| Unsure | **Unsure, re-measure** | Bad placement, motion, no stable pulse, a poor calibration, or a score near the boundary. No number is shown |

The app never shows an SpO2 value. It also shows heart rate and a quality score.

![From fingertip video to three states](docs/figures/ml_flow.png)

## The model in one paragraph

**Default engine (round 3): PhotonDistill v2.** A multilayer perceptron ({{phw2:seeds}} seeds of widths {{phw2:hidden}}, {{phw2:params}} parameters) on {{phw2:n_in}} causal window features relative to the person's own first minute, with heads for P(SpO2 < 90), SpO2 (not shown) and its own abstain output. It was trained in each fold from two teachers fitted on the training people only (the logistic chain on clean windows, a DC-colour regression on physics-simulated distant-flash copies). Only the student runs in the app. See [MODEL.md](MODEL.md) section 0 and `docs/figures/photon_architecture.png`.

**Previous engine (`?engine=hybrid`).** A **hybrid**: a physiological logistic chain (heart-rate rise, pulse shape and ratio-of-ratios features, each relative to the person's own first minute) gives a low-oxygen logit, and a **{{v:params}}-parameter 1D CNN** (`OxyNet`, three seeds, dependency-free JavaScript) learns a residual correction to it, with heart-rate, quality and experimental SpO2 heads. The network was pretrained self-supervised and warmed up on contact-oximeter data (OpenOximetry) before fine-tuning on phone video. Details: [MODEL.md](MODEL.md).

![Architecture](docs/figures/ml_architecture.png)

## Results, honestly (leave-one-person-out, nested selection, 95% person-bootstrap intervals)

The evaluation protocol was **pre-registered** (commit `{{v:prereg_commit}}`, [PREREGISTRATION.md](python/oxydrop_ml/PREREGISTRATION.md)) before any CNN result existed. A win needs the paired interval of the difference to the **best** honest baseline to exclude zero.

**P1 (primary, pre-registered): detect SpO2 < 90 on the six people of the UW Hoffman data, time-matched balanced accuracy.**

{{@p1_main}}

**The primary metric was not beaten.** The deployed pipeline R ({{hy:default_R:tm_bacc|full}}, optimistic because it was chosen after the outer scores were seen) and the nested per-person-selected hybrid ({{hy:HYBRID_FINAL:tm_bacc|full}}, the unbiased estimate of the selection procedure) both tie the shipped chain ({{b1:chain_v1:tm_bacc|full}}). The CNN alone ties it, and a chain refit with the same levers and no CNN has the higher point estimate, {{hy:CHAIN_SAME_LEVERS:tm_bacc|full}}. The CNN beats only weak baselines (ratio-of-ratios, clock), which is not a pre-registered win. One of three CNN seeds loses to the chain by itself.

**P2 (pre-registered metric, post hoc rule, exploratory): heart rate within 5 bpm, BUT PPG plus MTHS, 100 people.** Hybrid rule {{hp:all/HYBRID_agree:within5_full|full}} against {{hp:all/v2_spectral_acf__forced:within5_full|full}} for the v2 spectral estimator: paired difference {{hpd:all/v2_spectral_acf__forced|d}}. This is **not a clean win**: the rule was chosen after the pooled table had been seen (Amendment 3), and the gain comes from BUT PPG ({{hpd:butppg/v2_spectral_acf__forced|d}}). On MTHS the spectral estimator is nominally better ({{hp:mths/v2_spectral_acf__forced:within5_full}} against {{hp:mths/HYBRID_agree:within5_full}} for the rule, difference {{hpd:mths/v2_spectral_acf__forced|d}}), and on the Hoffman inner folds (the pooled out-of-fold windows of the six Hoffman people that were used to select the rule, not an outer-fold test result) the spectral estimator alone scores {{hr:spec:within5_full}} against {{hr:agree:within5_full}} for the rule that ships. Do not read this as a heart-rate improvement in general.

**P3 (pre-registered): absolute SpO2 on MTHS, MAE.** CNN {{ab:full/p23:p3_mae}} against {{b3:train_mean:mae}} for predicting the training mean: no skill. MTHS is normoxic, so SpO2 is not headlined and not shown to users.

What the experiments say about the network: **the OpenOximetry warm-up is the main source of its skill** (P1 {{ab:full/p23:p1_tm_bacc}} with it, {{ab:no_openox/p23k:p1_tm_bacc}} without); a device-agnostic-augmentation benefit is **not supported**; physics channels change nothing measurable; test-time BatchNorm adaptation hurts. Every lever, kept or dropped, is in the ledger in [MODEL.md](MODEL.md) and [WHITEPAPER.md](WHITEPAPER.md).

**Conformal three-state output (secondary, exploratory).** For the **deployed pipeline R** (the model the app runs; nested over people, thresholds from the five other people only) the declared level alpha = 0.10 gives {{cf:deployed_R/0.1:coverage|pct}} answered windows at {{cf:deployed_R/0.1:acc|pct}} accuracy, {{cf:deployed_R/0.1:alert_share_all|pct}} of all hypoxic windows alerted and {{cf:deployed_R/0.1:confident_miss|pct}} called Normal (target 10%). These rows are optimistic, because R was chosen with all six people in view; the nested per-person-selected hybrid gives {{cf:final/0.1:coverage|pct}}, {{cf:final/0.1:acc|pct}} and {{cf:final/0.1:alert_share_all|pct}}. **The chain-only control has the higher point estimates**: {{cf:chain_v1/0.1:coverage|pct}} answered at {{cf:chain_v1/0.1:acc|pct}} accuracy, {{cf:chain_v1/0.1:alert_share_all|pct}} alerted. At the coverage of the v1 band ({{v:v1_cov}}) the deployed pipeline scores {{cm:deployed_R/v1/conformal_mondrian:acc|pct}} against {{cm:deployed_R/v1/conformal_mondrian:reference_acc|pct}} ({{cm:deployed_R/v1/conformal_mondrian|d}} points, a tie by interval, not a win) and the chain control {{cm:chain_v1/v1/conformal_mondrian:acc|pct}}. The coverage guarantee holds roughly pooled and fails per person (person 1: {{cpp:deployed_R/0.1/hof_100001:confident_miss|pct}} of hypoxic windows called Normal).

**SpO2 on a contact oximeter, by skin tone (secondary, not a phone test).** On {{oxc:heldout_people}} held-out OpenOximetry people ({{oxc:heldout_people_with_sao2}} with blood-gas SaO2 labels) the CNN has MAE {{ox:lag_star/R:mae|full}} against {{ox:lag_star/ror_textbook:mae|full}} for the textbook ratio-of-ratios (tie, difference {{oxp:lag_star/R/ror_textbook|d}}) and {{ox:lag_star/train_mean:mae}} for the training mean; the learned label lag is {{oxl:ppg}} s {{oxl:ppg|ci}}. The dark-minus-light MAE gap by ITA tertile is {{oxg:ita/R/mae|d}} ({{oxg:ita/R/mae|n}} people); the Monk 7+ group has too few held-out people to estimate. The contact oximeter itself reads higher in darker skin: dark minus light {{oxb:monk|d}} points by Monk group and {{oxb:ita|d}} by ITA tertile. No SpO2 number is shown to users.

**Heart-rate voting (negative result).** A voting rule over autocorrelation, spectral and CNN estimates gives a clean-clip MAE of {{hv:butppg/vote+harmonic+octave+median5/clean:mae}} bpm on BUT PPG and {{hv:mths/vote+harmonic+octave+median5/clean:mae}} on MTHS (target under 3 bpm not met), is worse than the CNN alone on BUT PPG, and does not replace the P2 rule. For a resting pulse near 48 bpm the 51 bpm spectral floor gives MAE {{hvs:hof_100004/spec_band51:mae}} bpm and a 40 bpm floor {{hvs:hof_100004/spec_band40:mae}}; the CNN does not track that person.

{{@app_state}}

